## Logic

### Sheet1

#### Parameters

A row with a cell range stands for values next to each other that play one part.

| Cell | Name | Label | Value | Unit | Unit from | Read by |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| D1 |  | &lt;= on cell | 7 |  |  | 1 |
| E1 |  |  | 6 |  |  | 1 |
| F1 |  |  | Because it's in the Impossible that you find reality |  |  | 1 |
| A5:A8 |  |  | 0, 100, 50, -10 (4 values) |  |  | 1 each |

#### Formulas

A row with a count above 1 stands for one formula copied over its cells. It shows the first cell.

| Cells | Count | Formula | Reads | Role | Value | Math |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| A1 | 1 | `=LAMBDA(x, x+1)(5)` |  | constant | 6 | $`\operatorname{LAMBDA}(\mathrm{x}, \mathrm{x}+1)(5)`$ |
| A2 | 1 | `=LAMBDA(x,y, SQRT(x*x+y*y))(3,4)` |  | constant | 5 | $`\operatorname{LAMBDA}(\mathrm{x}, \mathrm{y}, \sqrt{\mathrm{x} \cdot \mathrm{x}+\mathrm{y} \cdot \mathrm{y}})(3, 4)`$ |
| F2 | 1 | `=CountWords(F1)` | F1 | result | 9 | $`\operatorname{CountWords}(\mathrm{F1})`$ |
| F4 | 1 | `=LET(area, LAMBDA(x,y,x*y), area(D1,E1))` | D1, E1 | result | 42 | $`\operatorname{LET}(\mathrm{area}, \operatorname{LAMBDA}(\mathrm{x}, \mathrm{y}, \mathrm{x} \cdot \mathrm{y}), \operatorname{area}(\mathrm{D1}, \mathrm{E1}))`$ |
| B5:B8 | 4 | `=Temperature(A5)` | A5 | result | -17.777777778 | $`\operatorname{Temperature}(\mathrm{A5})`$ |

